  "description": "model_diff.py defers module loading without checking can_defer_load, allowing sliced weight construction to copy unread storage.",
  "trigger": "Run eval/model_diff.py with an unquantized model whose MLP is sliced, using eligible deferred mt_fread weights. From commit 161, the earlier local-padding mismatch no longer masks this path. The usual quantized-versus-original comparison can encounter it on the original model.",
  "expected_behavior": "Respect module.can_defer_load before entering deferred loading, as the model loaders do.",
  "actual_behavior": "The script brackets every module without can_defer_load(). From 161, sliced get_tensor has no padding and no no_defer override: deferred loading allocates and queues the full weight, LinearFP16 cuts and copies from unread storage, and the later flush populates the original tensor rather than the retained copied slice. Comparison can silently use uninitialised slice weights. Source inspection only.",
